{"type":"standard","title":"Steven Horsford","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Steven Horsford</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q3514907","titles":{"canonical":"Steven_Horsford","normalized":"Steven Horsford","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Steven Horsford</span></span>"},"pageid":13272531,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Steven_Horsford_118th.jpeg/330px-Steven_Horsford_118th.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":412},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/61/Steven_Horsford_118th.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":1645,"height":2056},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1376701390","tid":"8448a302-b915-11f1-a2d7-405475635d9b","timestamp":"2026-09-25T19:15:49Z","description":"American politician (born 1973)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steven_Horsford","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steven_Horsford?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steven_Horsford?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Steven_Horsford"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steven_Horsford","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Steven_Horsford","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steven_Horsford?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Steven_Horsford"}},"extract":"Steven Alexzander Horsford is an American politician and businessman serving as the U.S. representative for Nevada's 4th congressional district since 2019, previously holding the position from 2013 to 2015. He also served as chair of the Congressional Black Caucus from 2023 to 2025. A member of the Democratic Party, he served in the Nevada State Senate, representing the 4th district, in Clark County, from 2005 to 2013. Horsford was the first African American to serve as Majority Leader (2009–2013) and the first African American to represent Nevada in Congress. He lost to Republican nominee Cresent Hardy in 2014.","extract_html":"<p><b>Steven Alexzander Horsford</b> is an American politician and businessman serving as the U.S. representative for Nevada's 4th congressional district since 2019, previously holding the position from 2013 to 2015. He also served as chair of the Congressional Black Caucus from 2023 to 2025. A member of the Democratic Party, he served in the Nevada State Senate, representing the 4th district, in Clark County, from 2005 to 2013. Horsford was the first African American to serve as Majority Leader (2009–2013) and the first African American to represent Nevada in Congress. He lost to Republican nominee Cresent Hardy in 2014.</p>"}